{"candidates":[{"content":"Add a parameterized trust threshold over attack edges: each edge carries a warrant strength (direct evidence, inferential, conjectural); for any threshold t, compute the grounded extension on the subgraph of edges with strength >= t. Prove the family is monotone in t, each extension is deterministic and polynomial, and committed roots remain valid because only edges are filtered, never added. This gives a principled way to expand skepticism by choosing t without changing the fixpoint operator.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"74fde5320d6c79520ea82d22a3e0c25a5ecc8e0cb50c3197058c5a3b0ecd2845"},{"role":"dependence","target":"c96a52fc060980a4742f93c9719f67bcaf0e3e60d1fd0d9f3a0d39c88af8caba"}],"typicality":0.35},{"content":"Introduce a dynamic re-computation protocol that, after an edge insertion or deletion, updates the grounded statuses incrementally by reusing the previous least fixpoint, with a change-propagation order that provably reaches the same fixpoint in polynomial total time. This makes the semantics responsive to new evidence without recomputing from scratch, and preserves determinism because the incremental result is defined as the unique least fixpoint of the updated graph.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"b25c49bfd4585cd0824221f7fd6fa154ffed828ad96ef4adc25fe3bed6b8517c"},{"role":"dependence","target":"cb5e696f588682056186b68681f9adbb9004427bd80c6e2a1dabb33dd6abb5fb"}],"typicality":0.4},{"content":"For every UNDECIDED node, compute its suspension margin: the minimum number of attack-edge deletions that would make it accepted under grounded semantics, using a polynomial-time sensitivity oracle over the final fixpoint rather than bounded-depth lookahead. This turns the binary suspension state into a graded diagnostic without promoting any node, thereby preserving the skeptical semantics and all guarantees.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"986d93e07b358fa8d689939883733eb3799f1d998665b237c764ba14fbaf9486"},{"role":"dependence","target":"b25c49bfd4585cd0824221f7fd6fa154ffed828ad96ef4adc25fe3bed6b8517c"}],"typicality":0.5},{"content":"Add a compositional interface: define an operation that combines two grounded-extension graphs by identifying a set of shared committed roots, and prove that the grounded extension of the union is the least fixed point of the combined operator and equals the join of the individual extensions when they agree on the shared roots. This enables modular expansion across schools while preserving determinism and root validity.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"74fde5320d6c79520ea82d22a3e0c25a5ecc8e0cb50c3197058c5a3b0ecd2845"}],"typicality":0.2},{"content":"Require every accepted node to carry a constructive grounded derivation certificate — a finite tree of attack/defense edges whose leaves are committed roots and whose internal nodes are IN by the grounded rules. The certificate is produced as a side output of the fixpoint and can be independently verified in polynomial time. This strengthens trust in committed roots without altering the semantics.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"986d93e07b358fa8d689939883733eb3799f1d998665b237c764ba14fbaf9486"},{"role":"dependence","target":"821e14232f7b43b22b767ff048e7d966d6a7d684ca90f20435a46762c621c52b"}],"typicality":0.45},{"content":"Define a refutation witness for each REFUTED node: a finite set of attacking chains such that no grounded defense can exist, certified by the absence of an IN defender at the fixpoint and by a monotone invariant that blocks any later reinstatement. This makes refutations checkable and supports a stronger external audit trail while preserving the existing fixpoint.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"821e14232f7b43b22b767ff048e7d966d6a7d684ca90f20435a46762c621c52b"}],"typicality":0.5}],"simulation_proposals":[]}